        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.875,
            0.021,
            0.96,
            0.039
          ],
          "content": "10/13/26"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.143,
            0.124,
            0.434,
            0.142
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "A Mathematical Example: Factorial"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.154,
            0.305,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": "• Non-recursive definition:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.173,
            0.334,
            0.19
          ],
          "content": "$n!=n \\times n-1 \\times \\ldots \\times 2 \\times 1$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.191,
            0.325,
            0.208
          ],
          "content": "= \\mathrm{n} (\\mathrm{n-1} \\times \\dots \\times 2 \\times 1)",
          "image_source": "images/page_0_equation_4.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.216,
            0.277,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "• Recursive definition:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.235,
            0.297,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "$n!=n(n-1)!$  for  $n\\geq0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.235,
            0.426,
            0.251
          ],
          "content": "**Recursive case**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.254,
            0.181,
            0.27
          ],
          "content": "$0! = 1$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.317,
            0.253,
            0.392,
            0.269
          ],
          "content": "**Base case**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.28,
            0.417,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "What happens if there is no base case?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.406,
            0.41,
            0.424
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Example: Fibonnaci Sequence"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.43,
            0.421,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": "• Sequence of numbers: 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13, ... a0 a1 a2 a3 a4 a5 a6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.46,
            0.409,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "§ Get the next number by adding previous two"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.476,
            0.222,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": "§ What is a8?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.493,
            0.276,
            0.509
          ],
          "content": "• Recursive definition:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.511,
            0.237,
            0.527
          ],
          "content": "$a_{n}=a_{n-1}+a_{n-2}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.263,
            0.51,
            0.366,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": "**Recursive Case**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.527,
            0.188,
            0.543
          ],
          "content": "§ a0 = 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.264,
            0.527,
            0.334,
            0.542
          ],
          "content": "**Base Case**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.544,
            0.188,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "§ a1 = 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.264,
            0.543,
            0.395,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": "**(another) Base Case**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.14,
            0.564,
            0.432,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": "Why did we need two base cases this time?"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.526,
            0.332,
            0.538,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": "2"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.576,
            0.124,
            0.846,
            0.142
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Factorial as a Recursive Function"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.152,
            0.633,
            0.168
          ],
          "content": "def factorial(n):"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.557,
            0.169,
            0.704,
            0.184
          ],
          "content": "\"\"\"Returns: factorial of n."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.558,
            0.185,
            0.67,
            0.2
          ],
          "content": "Pre: n ≥ 0 an int\"\"\""
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.712,
            0.153,
            0.829,
            0.195
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{array}{l} \\bullet \\mathrm{n! = n(n - 1)!} \\\\ \\bullet 0! = 1 \\end{array}",
          "image_source": "images/page_0_equation_28.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.558,
            0.202,
            0.616,
            0.217
          ],
          "content": "\\text {if} \\mathrm{n} = = 0:",
          "image_source": "images/page_0_equation_29.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.574,
            0.218,
            0.631,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "return 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.697,
            0.218,
            0.787,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": "<strong><u>Base case(s)</u></strong>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.558,
            0.25,
            0.691,
            0.267
          ],
          "content": "return n\\*factorial(n-1)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.734,
            0.356,
            0.75
          ],
          "content": "§ fib(n) has a stack that is always ≤ n"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.697,
            0.249,
            0.806,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": "<strong><u>Recursive case</u></strong>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.136,
            0.75,
            0.385,
            0.765
          ],
          "content": "§ But fib(n) makes a lot of redundant calls"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.716,
            0.326,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": "• Fibonacci is very inefficient."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.579,
            0.28,
            0.839,
            0.3
          ],
          "content": "What happens if there is no base case?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.574,
            0.406,
            0.848,
            0.423
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Fibonacci as a Recursive Function"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.715,
            0.435,
            0.876,
            0.45
          ],
          "content": "• Function that calls itself"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.54,
            0.435,
            0.62,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": "def fibonacci(n):"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.558,
            0.448,
            0.696,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": "\"\"\"Returns: Fibonacci no. a<sub>n</sub>"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.558,
            0.462,
            0.698,
            0.476
          ],
          "content": "Precondition: n ≥ 0 an int\"\"\""
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.732,
            0.451,
            0.865,
            0.465
          ],
          "content": "§ Each call is new frame"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.559,
            0.475,
            0.61,
            0.49
          ],
          "content": "if n <= 1:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.733,
            0.465,
            0.871,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": "§ Frames require memory"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.733,
            0.479,
            0.854,
            0.493
          ],
          "content": "§ ∞ calls = ∞ memory"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.574,
            0.49,
            0.625,
            0.505
          ],
          "content": "return 1"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.558,
            0.517,
            0.676,
            0.547
          ],
          "content": "return (fibonacci(n-1)+ fibonacci(n-2))"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.757,
            0.465,
            0.882
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_0_image_49.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.765,
            0.5,
            0.832,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": "fibonacci 3 n 5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.732,
            0.548,
            0.865,
            0.578
          ],
          "content": "fibonacci 1 <strong><u>fibonacci</u></strong> n 4 n 3"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.142,
            0.686,
            0.433,
            0.704
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Fibonacci: # of Frames vs. # of Calls"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.545,
            0.686,
            0.878,
            0.704
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Recursion is best for Divide and Conquer"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.716,
            0.818,
            0.733
          ],
          "content": "**Goal**: Solve problem P on a piece of data"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.69,
            0.741,
            0.736,
            0.758
          ],
          "content": "**data**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.764,
            0.868,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": "**Idea**: Split data into two parts and solve problem"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.629,
            0.785,
            0.692,
            0.804
          ],
          "content": "**data 1**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.615,
            0.82,
            0.811,
            0.836
          ],
          "content": "Solve Problem P Solve Problem P"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.662,
            0.853,
            0.765,
            0.87
          ],
          "content": "**Combine Answer!**"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.102,
            0.613,
            0.115,
            0.627
          ],
          "content": "3"
        },
