        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.564,
            0.123,
            0.858,
            0.143
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Three Steps for Divide and Conquer"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.154,
            0.794,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": "1. Decide what to do on “small” data"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.558,
            0.172,
            0.76,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "§ Some data cannot be broken up"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.557,
            0.188,
            0.792,
            0.204
          ],
          "content": "§ Have to compute this answer directly"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.205,
            0.792,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": "2. Decide how to break up your data"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.557,
            0.223,
            0.831,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": "§ Both “halves” should be smaller than whole"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.557,
            0.239,
            0.833,
            0.255
          ],
          "content": "§ Often no wrong way to do this (next lecture)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.539,
            0.256,
            0.818,
            0.273
          ],
          "content": "3. Decide how to combine your answers"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.558,
            0.274,
            0.808,
            0.29
          ],
          "content": "§ Assume the smaller answers are correct"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.558,
            0.29,
            0.829,
            0.307
          ],
          "content": "§ Combining them should give bigger answer"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.405,
            0.408,
            0.424
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Divide and Conquer Example"
        },
